WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.538
Why does this gate exist?

2
00:00:01.538 --> 00:00:04.354
Because accounts drift from the HR record,

3
00:00:04.354 --> 00:00:07.251
even after every earlier
gate is done right.

4
00:00:07.251 --> 00:00:09.737
A worker shows up in HR with no account.

5
00:00:09.737 --> 00:00:12.538
A terminated worker's
account is still enabled.

6
00:00:12.538 --> 00:00:14.849
An account turns up that nobody owns.

7
00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:17.763
Someone other than the named
writer changes a value.

8
00:00:17.763 --> 00:00:20.175
A card stays active after a separation.

9
00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:24.487
Each of those is a drift class, and
the run in this module finds them all.

10
00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:26.575
There's a second problem: time.

11
00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:30.541
Entra keeps its own logs for only
thirty days, and the evidence has

12
00:00:30.541 --> 00:00:34.875
to outlive the accounts it describes,
which are eventually disposed of.

13
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:38.676
So the findings and metrics
have to leave the directory,

14
00:00:38.676 --> 00:00:40.900
in a form an ISSO can check later.
